      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The risk of magnesium causing kidney stones is higher with very high doses (> 400mg) and especially in individuals with existing kidney issues. Taking 600-800mg may increase the risk significantly. However, a short-term, low to moderate dose (200-400mg) might be relatively safer for your kidneys. But, it's not recommended to gamble with your health. Consider reaching out to a nurse hotline or pharmacist for guidance on safer alternatives.",
